  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Suppose $\\theta$ is an acute angle and $\\tan\\theta+\\cot\\theta=8$. Find $\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt5}{2}$.\n\nUse $\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta=\\frac18$ and expand the square of the sum.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}8&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}+\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\8&=\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}\\\\8&=\\frac1{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta&=\\frac18\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)^2&=1+2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\\\(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)^2&=1+2\\left(\\frac18\\right)\\\\(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)^2&=\\frac54\\\\\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt5}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe positive root is required because $\\theta$ is acute.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
